#### integer to roman


class Solution {
    public String intToRoman(int num) {

        int[] values = {
            1000, 900, 500, 400,
            100, 90, 50, 40,
            10, 9, 5, 4, 1
        };

        String[] symbols = {
            "M", "CM", "D", "CD",
            "C", "XC", "L", "XL",
            "X", "IX", "V", "IV", "I"
        };

        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();

        for (int i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
            while (num >= values[i]) {
                num -= values[i];
                sb.append(symbols[i]);
            }
        }

        return sb.toString();
    }
}


for each roman value (13 values)
    while num >= value
Roman symbols are constant (13)

Worst case: number reduces step by step
TIME COMPLEXITY : O(1)
(Constant time — input size doesn’t grow)

SPACE COMPLEXITY : O(1)
